{"conversation_id":"ccc35339-416b-44a2-8e7a-771636b20152","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have applied the uniform fail-fast hardening via `publish-guest!` across all runtime and donor publication sites in `conformance.clj`, and restructured the error paths in `conformance.clj`, `exception_legs.clj`, and `exception_probes.clj` so that publication refusals are caught during dereference and delivered as per-backend `:error` results.\n\nI have launched the first authorized verification test (`clojure-to-python-test`) and will wait for it to finish.\n`clojure-to-python-test` completed with 9 failures / 0 errors (baseline-equal).\nI have launched the second authorized test (`python-to-php-test`) and will wait for it to complete.\n`python-to-php-test` completed with 6 failures / 18 errors (baseline-equal).\nI have launched the third authorized test (`php-provenance-test`) and will wait for it to complete.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-09 20:02:57 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-10 03:02:57 +07\n\n# Round 3 Resolution: Universal Publication Hardening \u0026 Per-Row Error Routing\n\n## 1. Summary of Actions\n\n1. **Finding 4 (Remaining Half) — Universal Fail-Fast Publication Hardening**:\n   - Implemented a uniform private helper [`publish-guest!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L50-L60) in [`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj).\n   - `publish-guest!` asserts `(when (= :refused (:status result)) (throw (ex-info ... result)))` immediately returning `result`.\n   - Wired uniformly across all kit publication sites:\n     - `published-php`\n     - `published-py`\n     - `published-clj`\n     - `publish-donor!`\n   - Prevents any guest module publication refusal from collapsing into a `nil` address.\n\n2. **Throw Reporting Path (P2 Resolution) — Per-Row Routing**:\n   - In [`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj), introduced `error-results` mapping `Throwable` instances across all vector VM backends (`:register`, `:semantic`, `:stack`). Wrapped `run-exception-program`'s publication resolution and execution in `try ... (catch Throwable e (error-results e))`.\n   - In [`test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj), wrapped `run-pair` and `run-leg` so that any `Throwable` thrown during donor dereference or execution is caught and delivered as `[id (kit/error-results e)]` across all scenario legs in the directed pair.\n   - In [`test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj), wrapped `run-frontend` and `run-fixture` so that any `Throwable` thrown during `boundary-donor` dereference or execution is caught and delivered as `[id (kit/error-results e)]` across all fixtures of that frontend.\n   - In `check-pair` and `check-frontend`, results enter the existing per-row loop:\n     - `(instance? Throwable actual)` is `true` for all three backends.\n     - `update-vals` captures `.getMessage` in `:host/error` and the complete refusal map in `:host/data`.\n     - `:status` maps to `{:register :error, :semantic :error, :stack :error}`.\n     - `do-report` logs individual per-backend operational failure errors for each row without aborting the `deftest`.\n\n3. **Correction Note on Round 2 Prose Mislabel**:\n   - Appended a correction note in the findings document clarifying that the 13 canonical PHP provenance rows in `exception_r0_results.edn:34-46` are the 6 Red Failure rows (`:php/fresh-named`, `:php/fresh-closure`, `:php/binding`, `:php/protocol-not-callable`, `:php/saved-protocol-not-callable`, `:php/forged-retention`) and 7 Error rows (`:php/protocol-invalid-invocation`, `:php/protocol-unsupported-binding`, `:php/local-reception`, `:php/foreign-reception`, `:php/retained-foreign-lifetime`, `:php/saved-protocol-invalid-invocation`, `:php/saved-protocol-unsupported-binding`), matching the verified aggregate counts of 18 failures and 21 errors.\n\n4. **Authorized Verification Runs**:\n   - `clojure-to-python-test`: Ran 1 tests containing 24 assertions. **9 failures, 0 errors** (baseline-equal).\n   - `python-to-php-test`: Ran 1 tests containing 24 assertions. **6 failures, 18 errors** (baseline-equal).\n   - `php-provenance-test`: Ran 1 tests containing 39 assertions. **18 failures, 21 errors** (baseline-equal).\n\n5. **Findings Document Updated**:\n   - Appended the Round 3 section to [`collab/exception-track/1794241000000-engineer-donor-link-absent.gemini-3.8-flash-high.findings.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794241000000-engineer-donor-link-absent.gemini-3.8-flash-high.findings.md#L450).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Unified Diffs\n\n### `test/yang/call/conformance.clj`\n```diff\ndiff --git a/test/yang/call/conformance.clj b/test/yang/call/conformance.clj\nindex 8cb2e908..a8bc2110 100644\n--- a/test/yang/call/conformance.clj\n+++ b/test/yang/call/conformance.clj\n@@ -47,10 +47,21 @@\n     [yin.vm :as vm]))\n \n \n+(defn- publish-guest!\n+  \"Publish guest module `spec` into the harness store, throwing immediately\n+   with `result` in ex-data if publication is refused.\"\n+  [spec]\n+  (let [result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n+    (when (= :refused (:status result))\n+      (throw (ex-info (str \"Guest module publication refused: \" (or (:reason result) (:status result)))\n+                      result)))\n+    result))\n+\n+\n (def ^:private published-php\n   \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n    `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n-  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n+  (delay (publish-guest!\n            (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                     (:call-address @h/published)))))\n \n@@ -58,7 +69,7 @@\n (def ^:private published-py\n   \"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\n    `yang.call` revision.\"\n-  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n+  (delay (publish-guest!\n            (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n \n@@ -66,7 +77,7 @@\n (def ^:private published-clj\n   \"`clj` published beside `js`, `php` and `py`, over the same host registry\n    and `yang.call` revision.\"\n-  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n+  (delay (publish-guest!\n            (clj-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                     (:call-address @h/published)))))\n \n@@ -187,6 +198,12 @@\n   (clj-prelude/admit (php-prelude/admit (h/registry))))\n \n \n+(defn- claims-call-sites?\n+  \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 call-site key anywhere.\"\n+  [ast]\n+  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n+\n+\n (defn publish-donor!\n   \"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\n    `xlang.donor.\u003cfrontend\u003e`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\n@@ -196,17 +213,20 @@\n   ([frontend source module]\n    (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit deps]} (profile frontend)\n          [refusal-key reason] refusal\n+         ast (let [raw (core-module/module-tree\n+                         [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n+                          (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))])]\n+               (cond-\u003e raw\n+                 (claims-call-sites? raw) u/annotate-call-sites))\n          spec (core-module/module-spec\n                 refusal-key reason (modules)\n                 {:name module,\n-                 :ast (core-module/module-tree\n-                        [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n-                         (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))]),\n+                 :ast ast,\n                  :exports '#{body},\n                  :runtime-name runtime,\n                  :runtime-address (address),\n                  :deps (if deps (deps) {})})\n-         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n+         result (publish-guest! spec)]\n      {:frontend frontend,\n       :module module,\n       :address (:address result),\n@@ -439,6 +459,12 @@\n       #(exception-outcome caller-frontend %))))\n \n \n+(defn error-results\n+  \"Map `e` across each vector VM backend as an operational failure.\"\n+  [e]\n+  (into (sorted-map) (map (fn [backend] [backend e]) (keys h/backends))))\n+\n+\n (defn run-exception-program\n   \"The exception probes' independent VM runs, concurrent on the JVM. Each\n    job owns its registry, task, link pair AND content-serving composition;\n@@ -447,17 +473,20 @@\n    clojure.test's :error reporting, NEVER relabelled as a guest condition.\n    All jobs settle even if one fails. `run-program` is unchanged.\"\n   [donor ast]\n-  ;; Resolve publication delays before starting independent readers.\n-  (link-source donor)\n-  (let [jobs (mapv (fn [backend]\n-                     [backend\n-                      (future\n-                        (try\n-                          (vm/value\n-                            (h/run-linked backend ast\n-                                          {:modules (modules)\n-                                           :link-source (link-source donor)}))\n-                          (catch Exception e e)))])\n-                   (keys h/backends))]\n-    (into (sorted-map)\n-          (map (fn [[backend job]] [backend @job])) jobs)))\n+  (try\n+    ;; Resolve publication delays before starting independent readers.\n+    (link-source donor)\n+    (let [jobs (mapv (fn [backend]\n                       [backend\n                        (future\n                          (try\n                            (vm/value\n                              (h/run-linked backend ast\n                                            {:modules (modules)\n                                             :link-source (link-source donor)}))\n                            (catch Exception e e)))])\n                      (keys h/backends))]\n       (into (sorted-map)\n             (map (fn [[backend job]] [backend @job])) jobs))\n     (catch Throwable e\n       (error-results e))))\n```\n\n### `test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj`\n```diff\ndiff --git a/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj b/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj\nindex a4cf7d02..bf792ee0 100644\n--- a/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj\n+++ b/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj\n@@ -211,12 +211,15 @@\n \n (defn run-leg\n   [{:keys [donor caller scenario] :as leg}]\n-  (let [published @(get published-donors donor)]\n-    (kit/run-exception-program\n-      published\n-      (kit/compose-exception published\n-                             (donor-exports donor)\n-                             caller (caller-source caller scenario)\n-                             (observation-form leg)))))\n+  (try\n+    (let [published @(get published-donors donor)]\n+      (kit/run-exception-program\n+        published\n+        (kit/compose-exception published\n+                               (donor-exports donor)\n+                               caller (caller-source caller scenario)\n+                               (observation-form leg))))\n+    (catch Throwable e\n+      (kit/error-results e))))\n \n \n (defn- probe-name\n@@ -244,19 +247,24 @@\n   [donor caller]\n   (let [pair-legs (filter #(and (= donor (:donor %)) (= caller (:caller %)))\n                           contract/pair-matrix)\n-        published @(get published-donors donor)\n-        observations (reduce\n-                       (fn [acc {:keys [scenario] :as leg}]\n-                         (list 'assoc acc scenario\n-                               (observation-form\n-                                 (assoc leg :probe-export (probe-name scenario)))))\n-                       {} pair-legs)\n-        results (kit/run-exception-program\n-                  published\n-                  (kit/compose-exception published\n-                                         (donor-exports donor)\n-                                         caller (batch-caller-source caller pair-legs)\n-                                         observations))]\n-    (if (some #(instance? Throwable %) (vals results))\n-      (into {} (for [{:keys [id] :as leg} pair-legs]\n-                 [id (run-leg leg)]))\n-      (into {} (for [{:keys [id scenario]} pair-legs]\n-                 [id (update-vals results #(get % scenario))])))))\n+    (try\n+      (let [published @(get published-donors donor)\n+            observations (reduce\n+                           (fn [acc {:keys [scenario] :as leg}]\n+                             (list 'assoc acc scenario\n+                                   (observation-form\n+                                     (assoc leg :probe-export (probe-name scenario)))))\n+                           {} pair-legs)\n+            results (kit/run-exception-program\n+                      published\n+                      (kit/compose-exception published\n+                                             (donor-exports donor)\n+                                             caller (batch-caller-source caller pair-legs)\n+                                             observations))]\n+        (if (some #(instance? Throwable %) (vals results))\n+          (into {} (for [{:keys [id] :as leg} pair-legs]\n+                     [id (run-leg leg)]))\n+          (into {} (for [{:keys [id scenario]} pair-legs]\n+                     [id (update-vals results #(get % scenario))]))))\n+      (catch Throwable e\n+        (let [err (kit/error-results e)]\n+          (into {} (for [{:keys [id]} pair-legs]\n+                     [id err])))))))\n```\n\n### `test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj`\n```diff\ndiff --git a/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj b/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\nindex 19a29ef3..bedb3abc 100644\n--- a/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\n+++ b/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\n@@ -163,11 +163,14 @@\n   